.TH PVE-SMART-ALERT 8 "2026-10-17" "pve-smart-alert" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
pve-smart-alert \- SMART drive alerts for Proxmox VE
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pve-smart-alert
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B pve-smart-alert check
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.br
.B pve-smart-alert scan
.br
.B pve-smart-alert status
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B pve-smart-alert doctor
.br
.B pve-smart-alert config check
.br
.B pve-smart-alert config show
.RB [ \-\-defaults ]
.br
.B pve-smart-alert test\-notification
.RB [ \-\-severity
.IR severity ]
.RB [ \-\-transport
.IR transport ]
.br
.B pve-smart-alert dump\-fixture
.RB [ \-\-output
.IR directory ]
.RB { \-\-all | \fIdevice\fR\ ...}
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pve-smart-alert
reads the SMART data of every drive of a Proxmox VE host with
.BR smartctl (8),
evaluates it against a catalog of checks, and reports problems through the
notification system of Proxmox VE, with mail to root as the fallback.
A problem is reported once, again when it gets worse, as a reminder after a
while, and when it has cleared.
.PP
The package runs
.B pve-smart-alert check
from the systemd timer
.BR pve-smart-alert.timer ,
3 minutes after boot and then 30 minutes after the start of the previous
run.
The tool only reads from drives; it never enables SMART, starts a self-test
or changes a setting of a drive, and it changes no file on the host except
its own.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Run one check: find and read the drives, evaluate them, compare the result
with the state of earlier runs, send the notifications that are due and save
the state.
The first run sends one summary of the drives it monitors.
With
.BR \-\-dry\-run ,
print the findings and the notifications a run would send now, and send and
change nothing.
.TP
.B scan
Find the drives of the host, read each of them once, and show every device
found with its source (the device scan of smartctl, the probe for HPE Smart
Array controllers, or a manual entry) and what became of it: monitored, in
standby, unreadable, or skipped with a reason.
For a drive it shows model, serial number, class, what uses it, its wear
value with the source and, behind a RAID controller, the controller and the
device ID.
A controller whose drives smartctl cannot read is named above the devices.
.TP
.B status
Show, from the stored state, the last run and every drive with its active
conditions.
Nothing is read from a drive.
With
.BR \-\-json ,
print the state as JSON.
.TP
.B doctor
Report one line for each part of the host the tool works with: the
configuration, smartctl, the notify bridge, the templates, the mail command,
the routing of the notifications and of the fallback mail, the state, the
timer, the Proxmox VE version, smartd, the controllers and the HPE probe.
Each line is
.BR ok ,
.BR warn ,
.B fail
or
.BR skip ,
with advice where something can be done.
.TP
.B config check
Validate the configuration file.
An error names the key and the line.
.TP
.B config show
Print every key with its effective value and where the value comes from, the
file or the built-in default.
With
.BR \-\-defaults ,
print the built-in defaults.
.TP
.B test\-notification
Send one test notification and report what the notification system did with
it, and which matchers route it.
.B \-\-severity
is one of
.BR info " (the default), " notice ", " warning " and " error .
.B \-\-transport
is one of
.BR auto ", " pve\-notify " and " mail ,
and replaces the configured transport for this test.
.TP
.B dump\-fixture
Record the device scan, lsblk and the output of smartctl for every device
found
.RB ( \-\-all )
or for the named devices, as one archive in the current directory or in
.BR \-\-output .
Serial numbers, WWNs and UUIDs are replaced by placeholders; nothing is
written when a real value would be left.
Model names, firmware versions and the node name are kept: look at the
archive before you share it.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration is
.IR /etc/pve\-smart\-alert/config.toml ,
in TOML.
Every key is optional; without the file the defaults apply.
.I /usr/share/doc/pve\-smart\-alert/config.reference.toml
lists every key with its default and explains it.
A file that does not validate never stops a run: the last configuration that
passed is used, or the defaults, and the problem is reported as
.BR tool.config_invalid .
.PP
The sections are
.B [smartctl]
(path, timeout and detail level),
.B [discovery]
(exclude rules, the HPE probe and manual devices in
.BR [[discovery.device]] ),
.B [notify]
and
.B [notify.reminder]
(transport and notification policy),
.B [checks."\fIcheck\-id\fB"]
(thresholds, enabled state and confirmation count of a check, and the
enabled state of a condition of the tool), and
.B [[drive]]
(overrides for one drive, selected by model pattern, serial number or WWN).
.PP
The interval of the timer is not a key of this file; change it with
.BR "systemctl edit pve\-smart\-alert.timer" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed.
For
.BR check ,
whatever the health of the drives.
.TP
.B 1
A problem: for
.BR check ,
a notification could not be handed over and is planned again on the next
run, or the run failed; for
.BR "check \-\-dry\-run" ,
the drives have findings; for
.BR scan ,
the device scan failed; for
.BR doctor ,
a line failed; for
.BR "config check" ,
the file is invalid.
.TP
.B 2
Wrong use of the command line, or a configuration that prevents the command.
.TP
.B 3
For
.BR check ,
another run holds the lock; the timer counts this as success.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/pve\-smart\-alert/config.toml
The configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/pve\-smart\-alert/state.json
The state: what was reported and when.
Deleting it makes the next run a first run.
.TP
.I /var/lib/pve\-smart\-alert/last\-good\-config.json
The last configuration that passed validation.
.TP
.I /run/pve\-smart\-alert/
The lock of a run and the stamp of the failure mail.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/pve\-smart\-alert/notify\-bridge
The program that hands a notification to the notification system of
Proxmox VE.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/pve\-smart\-alert/config.reference.toml
The reference configuration.
.SH NOTIFICATIONS
Every notification has the type
.B pve\-smart\-alert
and the fields
.B type
and
.BR hostname ;
one about a single drive also
.BR event ,
.BR device ,
.B serial
and
.BR model ,
and a drive behind a MegaRAID or HPE Smart Array controller
.BR device\-id .
A matcher with
.B match\-field regex:type=^pve\-smart\-alert$
selects all of them.
.B pve-smart-alert doctor
warns when a severity of the tool reaches no target.
.PP
When a run fails, a short mail to root says so, at most once a day and once
more after a reboot.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smartctl (8),
.BR smartd (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
.PP
The README, the check catalog and the hardware support table of the source
repository.
